#[No]	[Cause]	[Investigated actions]	[Corrective actions]

A.020,	"Parameter Checksum Error",
	"The power supply voltage suddenly dropped.",	"Measure the power supply voltage.",	"Set the power supply voltage within the specified range, and set Fn005 to initialize the parameters.",
	"The power supply went off while changing parameter setting.",	"Note the circumstances when the power supply went off.",	 "Set Fn005 to initialize the parameters and then set the parameters again.",
	"The number of times that parameters were written exceeds the limit.",	"Were the parameters frequently changed through the host controller?",	 "The Servopack may be faulty. Repair or replace the Servopack. Reconsider the method of writing parameters.",
	"Malfunction caused by noise from the AC power supply or grounding line, static electricity noise, etc.",	"Turn the power supply off and on several times. If the alarm still occurs, there may be noise interference.",	"Take counter measures against noise.",
	"Gas, water drops, or cutting oil entered the Servopack and caused failure of the internal component.",	 "Check the installation conditions.",	 "The Servopack may be faulty. Repair or replace the Servopack.",
	"A Servopack fault occurred.",	"Turn the power supply off and on several times. If the alarm still occurs, the Servopack is faulty.",	"The Servopack may be faulty. Repair or replace the Servopack.",
A.021,	"Parameter Format Error",
	"The software version of the Servopack that caused an alarm is older than that of the the written parameters.",	"Check the software version display (Fn012) to see if the set software version agrees with that of the Servopack. If not, an alarm may occur.",	"Write the parameters of another Servopack of the same model with the same software version.Then turn the power off and then on again.",
	"A Servopack fault occurred.",	"-",	"The Servopack may be faulty. Repair or replace the Servopack.",
