A.400,	"Overvoltage",
	"100-VAC SERVOPACK:AC power voltage exceeded 145V.200-VAC SERVOPACK:AC power voltage exceeded 290V.400-VAC SERVOPACK:AC power voltage exceeded 580V.200-VAC SERVOPACK:DC power voltage exceeded 410V.400-VAC SERVOPACK:DC power voltage exceeded 820V.",	"Measure the power supply voltage.",	"Set AC power supply voltage within the specified range.",
	"The power supply is unstable, or was influenced by a lightning surge.",	"Measure the power supply voltage.",	"Improve the power supply conditions by installing a surge protector, etc. Then, turn the power supply on again. If the alarm still occurs, the Servopack may be faulty. Repair or replace the Servopack.",
	"Voltage for AC power supply was too high during acceleration or deceleration.",	"Check the power supply voltage and the speed and torque/force during operation.",	"Set AC power supply voltage within the specified range.",
	"The external regenerative resistance is too high for the actual operation conditions.",	"Check the operation conditions and the regenerative resistance.",	"Check the operation condition including overload, and reconsider the regenerative resistor value.",
	"The load moment of inertia (mass) exceeded the allowable value., Confirm that the load moment of inertia (mass) ratio is within the allowable range.",	"Increase the deceleration time, or reduce the load.",
