	"An encoder fault occurred.",	"-",	"Turn the power supply off and then on again. If the alarm still occurs, the servomotor may be faulty. Repair or replace the servomotor.",
	"A Servopack fault occurred.",	"-",	"Turn the power supply off and then on again. If the alarm still occurs, the Servopack may be faulty. Repair or replace the Servopack.",
A.Cb0,	"Encoder Echoback Error",
	"The encoder wiring and contact are incorrect.",	"Check the encoder wiring.",	"Correct the encoder wiring.",
	"Noise interference occurred due to incorrect encoder cable specifications.",	"-",	"Use tinned annealed copper twisted-pair or shielded twisted-pair cable with a core of at least 0.12 mm2.",
	"Noise interference occurred because the wiring distance for the encoder cable is too long.",	"-",	"The wiring distance must be 20m (65.6 ft) max.",
	"The FG potential varies because of influence from machines on the servomotor side, such as welder.",	"Check the encoder cable and connector.",	"Properly ground the device to separate from the encoder FG.",
	"Excessive vibration and shocks were applied to the encoder.",	"Check the operating environment.",	"Reduce the machine vibration or correctly install the servomotor.",
	"An encoder fault occurred.",	"-",	"Turn the power supply off and then on again. If the alarm still occurs, the servomotor may be faulty. Repair or replace the servomotor.",
	"A Servopack fault occurred.",	"-",	"Turn the power supply off and then on again. If the alarm still occurs, the Servopack may be faulty. Repair or replace the Servopack.",
A.CC0,	"Multiturn Limit Disagreement",
	"When using a direct-drive (DD) servomotor, the multi-turn limit value (Pn205) is different from that of the encoder.",	"Check Pn205.",	"Correct the setting of Pn205 (0 to 65535).",
	"The multi-turn limit value of the encoder is different from that of the Servopack. Or, the multi-turn limit value of the Servopack has been changed.",	"Check Pn205 of the Servopack.",	"Execute Fn013 at the occurrence of alarm.",
	"A Servopack fault occurred.",	"-",	"Turn the power supply off and then on again. If the alarm still occurs, the Servopack may be faulty. Repair or replace the Servopack.",
A.CF1,	"Reception Failed Error in Feedback Option Module Communications",
	"Wiring of cable between the serial converter unit and the Servopack is incorrect or contact is faulty.",	"Check the external encoder wiring.",	"Correct the cable wiring.",
	"The specified cable is not used between the serial converter unit and the Servopack.",	"Check the external encoder wiring specifications.",	"Use the specified cable.",
	"The cable between the serial converter unit and the Servopack is too long.",	"Measure the external encoder cable length.",	"Use 20-m cable max.",
	"The sheath of cable between the serial converter unit and the Servopack is broken.",	"Check the external encoder cable.",	"Replace the cable.",
A.CF2,	"Timer Stopped Error in Feedback Option Module Communications",
	"Noise interference with the cable between the serial converter unit and the Servopack.",	"-",	"Correct the wiring around the serial converter unit, e.g., separating the input/output signal line from main circuit cable or grounding.",
	"A serial converter unit fault occurred.",	"-",	"Replace the serial converter unit.",
	"A Servopack fault occurred.",	"-",	"Replace the Servopack.",
A.d00,	"Position Deviation Overflow",
	"The contact in the servomotor U, V, and W wiring is faulty.",	"Check the servomotor main circuit cable connection.",	"Confirm that there is no contact fault in the motor wiring or encoder wiring.",
	"The Servopack gain is too low.",	"Check the Servopack gain to see if it is too low.",	"Increase servo gain using the parameters such as Pn100 and Pn102.",
	"The position reference pulse frequency is too high.",	"Reduce the reference pulse frequency, and operate the Servopack.",	"Reduce the position reference pulse frequency or reference acceleration. Or, reconsider the electronic gear ratio.",
	"The position reference acceleration is too fast.",	"Reduce the reference acceleration, and operate the Servopack.",	"Apply the smoothing function, such as using position reference acceleration/deceleration time constant (Pn216).",
	"The setting of the parameter Pn520 (Excessive Position Error Alarm Level) is low against the operating condition.",	"Check the excessive position error alarm level (Pn520) to see if it is set to an appropriate value.",	"Set the parameter Pn520 to a correct value.",
	"A Servopack fault occurred.",	"-",	"Turn the power supply off and then on again. If the alarm still occurs, the Servopack may be faulty. Repair or replace the Servopack.",
A.d01,	"Position Deviation Overflow Alarm at Servo ON",
	"When setting not to clear position error pulses, the servomotor rotated while the servo was off, resulting in position error pulse overflow.",	"Check the error counter (position error amount) (Un008) while servo is off .",	"Set position error to be cleared while the servomotor power is OFF. Or, correct the excessive position error alarm level at servo ON (Pn526).",
A.d02,	"Position Deviation Overflow Alarm for Speed Limit at Servo ON",
	"The servo was turned on while the position error pulses accumulated, and the reference pulse was input while the motor was running at the speed limit(Pn529). As a result, the position error count exceeded the excessive position error alarm level(Pn520).",	"Check the error counter (position error amount) (Un008) while servo is off .",	"Set position error pulses to be cleared while in servo off status. Or, correct the excessive position error alarm level (Pn520). Or, adjust the speed limit level (Pn529) when servo turns on.",
A.d10,	"Motor-Load Position Deviation Overflow",
	"The motor rotation direction and scale installation direction are opposite.",	"Check the servomotor rotation direction and the scale installation direction.",	"Install the scale in the opposite direction, or reverse the setting of the external encoder usage method (Pn002.3).",
	"Mounting of the load (e.g., stage) and scale joint installation are incorrect.",	"Check the scale mechanical connection.",	"Check the mechanical joints.",
A.d30,	"Position Data Overflow",
	"The position data exceeded ¡¾1879048192.",	"Check the input reference pulse counter (Un00C).",	"Reconsider the operation conditions.",
